contentText:
This week, Billboard’s New Music Latin poll — curated with key recommendations by Billboard Latin and Billboard Español editors — features new music including Farruko’s “Madrid,” Yuridia’s “Que Se Vaya” and Pepe Aguilar’s new live album recorded during his concert at the Hollywood Bowl, to name a few.&nbsp;

Notably, Los Ángeles Azules and TINI teamed up on a second collaboration called “Pa’ Él,” which blends the Mexican group’s signature cumbia sonidera sound with the Argentine&#8217;s pop vocal delicacy. “This one’s for him/ For the liar who didn’t know how to love me,” TINI chants in the chorus.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

“I deeply admire how Los Ángeles Azules have managed to connect with so many generations through their music,” she said in a statement. The Mexican group added: “We hope audiences embrace it with the same love we put into creating it, and most of all, that they enjoy it and dance to it.”

Meanwhile, artists such as Myke Towers and El De La Tinta have also dropped new music this week.&nbsp;

The most recent New Music Latin poll (published on Aug. 14) was topped by Carín León and Ke Personaje’s “Qué Andas Haciendo,” which earned nearly 60% of the vote. Which release this week do you think is best? Give these new releases a spin and vote for your favorite new Latin music release below.

Editor’s Note: The results of the weekly New Music Latin poll will be posted if the poll generates more than 1,000 votes. This poll closes at 11 a.m. ET on Monday (Aug. 24).

